# Test: IS-IS DIS pseudo-node LSP wire format (spec-isis-8 DIS / broadcast).
#
# VALIDATES: spec-isis-8-dis-broadcast -- the pseudo-node LSP the elected
#            Designated IS originates on a broadcast LAN (ISO/IEC 10589 clause
#            8.4.5) decodes end-to-end through the user-facing `ze isis-decode`
#            CLI: an L1 LSP whose LSP ID carries a NON-ZERO pseudonode octet (the
#            LAN ID <system-id>.<pseudonode-id>) and whose Extended IS
#            Reachability TLV 22 lists every router on the segment as a neighbor
#            at metric 0 (Users Stories 1, 2: the LAN collapses to a star with the
#            pseudo-node at the center). This is AC-3 over the wire.
# PREVENTS:  a regression where the pseudo-node LSP is built with a zero
#            pseudonode octet (indistinguishable from a router LSP), omits a
#            member, or advertises a non-zero member metric.
#
# The fixture below is PINNED to the codec by
# internal/plugins/isis/packet/pseudonode_ci_test.go
# (TestISISPseudonodeCIFixtureDecodes): if a codec/encoder change alters the
# bytes, that Go test fails alongside this .ci, so the functional fixture and the
# build path cannot drift.
#
# Live DIS election (three Ze nodes on a shared broadcast segment electing one
# DIS, the DIS originating the pseudo-node LSP listing all members, every node's
# own LSP pointing at the pseudo-node as a single TLV 22 entry, DIS-loss
# re-election, and the LAN CSNP cadence) needs raw L2 (AF_PACKET) on a Linux veth
# and is proven by:
#   - the in-memory engine wiring tests (run on any host, including darwin):
#     TestISISDISElection (three nodes elect one DIS, pseudo-node flooded
#     everywhere), TestOwnLSPPointsAtPseudoNode (the star encoding),
#     TestISISDISReElectOnLoss (DIS loss re-elects), TestISISDISYieldPurgesPseudonode
#     (a higher-priority join transfers the role and the old DIS purges), and the
#     pure-logic election + pseudo-node unit tests
#     (internal/plugins/isis/circuit/dis_test.go,
#     internal/plugins/isis/lsdb/pseudonode_test.go); and
#   - the QEMU integration tests + the FRR interop scenario isis-lan-dis-frr
#     (owned by spec-isis-13).
# This functional test exercises the pseudo-node LSP wire format only: hex PDU ->
# ze isis-decode -> JSON.

# --- L1 pseudo-node LSP: non-zero pseudonode LAN ID + 3 members at metric 0. ----
# LAN ID 0000.0000.0001.07 (pseudonode octet 0x07), fragment 0, seq 1, lifetime
# 1200; TLV 22 lists 0000.0000.0001 / 0000.0000.0002 / 0000.0000.0003 at metric 0.
stdin=isis-pn:hex=831b010612010000003e04b0000000000001070000000001e3d4011621000000000001000000000000000000000200000000000000000000030000000000
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze isis-decode:stdin=isis-pn
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains="type":"l1-lsp"
expect=stdout:contains="lsp-id":"0000.0000.0001.07-00"
expect=stdout:contains="sequence-number":1
expect=stdout:contains="checksum-valid":true
expect=stdout:contains="type":22
expect=stdout:contains="value":"000000000001000000000000000000000200000000000000000000030000000000"
